<Wiki
  title="puv sync"
  description="Install exactly puv.lock. Sync does not resolve."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>sync</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv sync</code> installs the lock. It is the same install as
    <a href="/wiki/commands/install"><code>puv install</code></a> with no arguments.
  </p>

  <h2>A clean tree</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv sync</pre>
  <p>
    Every package in <code>puv.lock</code> is linked into <code>.puv/deps/</code> from the
    content-addressed cache. Missing archives are downloaded. A download prints a progress line
    on stderr. A cached archive stays quiet.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is the second step after <a href="/wiki/commands/contain"><code>puv contain</code></a>
    when you imported a Composer lock and want those bytes on disk without a new solve.
  </p>

  <h2>A drifted manifest</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv sync</pre>
  <p>
    If <code>puv.toml</code> and <code>puv.lock</code> disagree, sync stops and tells you to run
    <a href="/wiki/commands/lock"><code>puv lock</code></a>. It does not resolve on its own.
  </p>
  <pre class="block"># puv.toml requires symfony/console, the lock does not
puv sync
puv lock
puv sync</pre>
  <p>
    <code>.puv/lockb</code> is a cache of the parsed lock so a later sync can skip re-reading it.
    If the bytes of <code>puv.lock</code> change, <code>lockb</code> is discarded. It is not a
    second source of truth. The files are drawn on <a href="/wiki/files">files</a>.
  </p>
</Wiki>
